1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,358
A dragon's egg has to stay

2
00:00:01,358 --> 00:00:02,611
warm for three months.

3
00:00:02,775 --> 00:00:04,226
But if a three-ton mother sits

4
00:00:04,226 --> 00:00:04,748
on it,

5
00:00:04,795 --> 00:00:06,059
she crushes it flat.

6
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:07,731
So you don't sit on it.

7
00:00:07,941 --> 00:00:09,752
You bury it in warm volcanic

8
00:00:09,752 --> 00:00:10,332
ash,

9
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:12,120
just like the maleo bird does.

10
00:00:12,632 --> 00:00:14,130
But lava is over a thousand

11
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:14,918
degrees.

12
00:00:15,128 --> 00:00:16,451
Bury it too close,

13
00:00:16,463 --> 00:00:17,450
and your egg is cooked in

14
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,192
seconds.

15
00:00:18,356 --> 00:00:19,482
So you test the ground with

16
00:00:19,482 --> 00:00:20,270
your snout,

17
00:00:20,283 --> 00:00:22,233
like a malleefowl checking its nest,

18
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:24,137
until you find the perfect spot:

19
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,506
thirty-four degrees.

20
00:00:25,844 --> 00:00:27,168
But now your egg is buried

21
00:00:27,168 --> 00:00:28,618
under a metre of ash.

22
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:30,615
How does the baby breathe?

23
00:00:31,127 --> 00:00:32,288
So the shell is covered in

24
00:00:32,288 --> 00:00:33,947
thousands of tiny pores.

25
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,213
Air gets in,

26
00:00:35,213 --> 00:00:36,675
and stale air gets out.

27
00:00:37,106 --> 00:00:38,383
But that shell is as hard

28
00:00:38,383 --> 00:00:39,137
as stone.

29
00:00:39,648 --> 00:00:40,948
The baby is trapped.

30
00:00:41,703 --> 00:00:42,957
So it grows a tiny egg

31
00:00:42,957 --> 00:00:43,851
tooth on the tip of its

32
00:00:43,851 --> 00:00:44,465
snout,

33
00:00:44,478 --> 00:00:45,755
just like a baby crocodile,

34
00:00:45,755 --> 00:00:47,020
and chips its way out.

35
00:00:47,531 --> 00:00:49,168
And it never meets its mother.

36
00:00:49,679 --> 00:00:50,852
It digs up through the ash

37
00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:51,455
alone,

38
00:00:51,537 --> 00:00:52,825
shakes itself off,

39
00:00:52,988 --> 00:00:54,614
and flies on its very first

40
00:00:54,614 --> 00:00:55,321
day.

